1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:29,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ladies and gentlemen, the hearing of the Committee on Finance, Subcommittee G, is hereby called to order. Our hearing for today is the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget of the Department of Justice and its attached agencies. We would like to acknowledge the presence of Senator Ping Lacson.

2
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:41,700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We now call on our committee secretary, Attorney Lina, to acknowledge and place on record our resource persons. Attorney Lina, you have the floor.

3
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:59,980
Committee Secretary: Good morning, Mr. Chair. Good morning, Senator Lacson, sir. From the DOJ family, we have the following in attendance: Secretary Frederick A. Vida; Undersecretary Raul T. Vasquez.

4
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:29,980
Committee Secretary: Undersecretary Margarita N. Gutierrez; Undersecretary Deo L. Marco; Undersecretary Nicolas Felix L. Ty; Undersecretary Gard M. Candelaria; Prosecutor General Richard Anthony D. Fadullon; Chief State Counsel Dennis Arvin L. Chan; from the Bureau of Immigration, Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado.

5
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:34,840
Committee Secretary: From the Land Registration Authority, we have Gerardo P. Sirios, Administrator.

6
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:39,620
Committee Secretary: From the National Bureau of Investigation, Melvin A. Matiwag, the Director.

7
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:46,140
Committee Secretary: From the Office of the Government Corporate Council, Solomon M. Hermosura.

8
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:56,180
Committee Secretary: From the Office for Alternative Dispute Resolution, we have Jose Maria R. Palaganas, Executive Director.

9
00:05:56,180 --> 00:06:01,740
Committee Secretary: From the Parole and Probation Authority, Wilson R. Suba, Administrator.

10
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:09,340
Committee Secretary: From the Presidential Commission on Good Government, Justice Melchor Quirino C. Sadang, the Chairperson.

11
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:16,220
Committee Secretary: From the Bureau of Corrections, General Gregorio P. Catapang, Jr., Director General.

12
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:23,820
Committee Secretary: From the Department of Budget and Management, Representatives to the DOJ, Mr. Carlos M. Castro, Director.

13
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:29,540
Committee Secretary: From the COA to the DOJ, Attorney.

14
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:35,380
Committee Secretary: Gumer Guime, Cassandra Conde, and Imelda Baguiza.

15
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:37,140
Committee Secretary: That's all for now, Mr. Chair. Thank you.

16
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:41,660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Attorney Lina. We will now proceed with our opening statement.

17
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:59,460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Actually, 25 years ago, it's full circle for this representation because I first defended the DOJ budget 25 years ago as Chairman then of the Committee on Justice here in the Senate.

18
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:09,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And so I'm back as Senate Committee on Justice Chairperson, and 25 years later, I will be defending your budget.

19
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:22,580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 25 years ago, kami po ni Senator Ping Lacson ay sabay na halal bilang senador. In fact, I call him my mista in the Senate, batch 2001.

20
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:26,020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And he's here with us also today.

21
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:29,160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ngayong araw, gusto natin sukatin ang...

22
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Proposed 2027 Budget ng DOJ at ng attached agencies nito.

23
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:40,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sukatin natin ang 43.3 billion pesos sa tanong ng karaniwang Pilipino.

24
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:46,580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kaya ba nitong ibigay ang mabilis, abot kaya, makatao, at pantay na hustisya?

25
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:50,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kaya bang managot ang dapat managot?

26
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:55,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sabi nga, 43.3 billion pesos ang gagasusin natin.

27
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:58,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Habang base sa COA...

28
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:07,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tapos, 1.3 trillion naman ang pondo ng gobernong ninanakaw taon-taon.

29
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:19,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kaya, napakahalaga ng sistema ng katarungan sa ating bansa para matugunan ang nais ng ating mga kababayan.

30
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:25,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: May dagdag na pondo para sa National Prosecution Service Bureau of Corrections.

31
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Public Attorney's Office.

32
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:29,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Makakatulong ang mga pondong ito.

33
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:38,800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Para marinig ang mga biktima, mabigyan ng abogado ang mga mahihirap, at matiyak na makatao at ang pagtrato sa mga nakakulong.

34
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:43,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pero bumaba naman ng 23% ang budget ng NBI.

35
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:48,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kabilang ang halos 90% na bawas sa capital outlay.

36
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:50,220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay lang ba yun?

37
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:57,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Habang lumalala at nagiging mas komplikado ang cybercrime, mga scams, human trafficking,

38
00:08:57,940 --> 00:08:59,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: at malalaking financial crimes.

39
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:04,660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang batas, ang software ng bansa.

40
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:10,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang justice system naman, ang operating system for ang hardware.

41
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:20,320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kung kulang sa mga investigador, prosecutor, mga field office, at luma na ang forensic tools at case tracking systems,

42
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:23,180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: kahit gaano kaganda ang software.

43
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:29,180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kung ang operating system ay 486.

44
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:33,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Or something, yung mga panahon namin,

45
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:37,800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Eh, mapuprotektahan ba ang mga maliliit na ating mga kababayan?

46
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:41,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Halimbawa, tulad ng mga magsasaka sa agriculture smuggling,

47
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:46,120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: o ang ating mga anak laban sa online sexual abuse and exploitation.

48
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Mabigat ang pasan ng ating DOJ.

49
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:58,320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sa 45 agriculture economic sabotage complaints, halimbawa, na na-refer sa DOJ hanggang May of this year,

50
00:09:58,840 --> 00:09:59,360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 35!

51
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:09,500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang binalik para sa case build-up, 35 of 45 returned for additional case build-up.

52
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:14,480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Nilalamo ng agriculture smuggling halimbawa ang kabuhayan ng mga magsasaka,

53
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:21,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: mga ngingisda, at patuloy na mataas ang presyo ng pagkain at patuloy ang gutom.

54
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:27,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pero nasaan ang mga forfeiture ng mga nagwawasak ng ating agriculture economy?

55
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Nasaan ang mga conviction?

56
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:34,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sa pang-aabuso sa mga bata, inaasahang kumilos agad ang Estado.

57
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:38,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Pero bumaba sa halos 35.7 million pesos

58
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:45,660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang proposed allocation para sa National Coordination Center against OSAEC and CISAEM.

59
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:51,260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 61% lower kaysa sa 2026 enacted level.

60
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:57,420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Samantala, uulitin natin 90% ang bawas sa capital outlay ng NBI

61
00:10:57,420 --> 00:11:03,960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: at 898 sa mga authorized positions ito na nanatiling bakante.

62
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:12,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang 2027 DOJ budget dapat maging kongkretong commitment na punan ang mga bakanting posisyon,

63
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:18,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: bigyan ng sapat na kagamitan ang mga investigador, pagdugtong-dugtongin ang mga ahensya.

64
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:25,480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Bumuoon ng mga matibay na kasong ilalatag sa korte, protektahan ng mga biktima,

65
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: panagutin ang mga

66
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:27,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: salarin.

67
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:31,360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Secretary Vida and the rest of the team DOJ,

68
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:37,240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: today we invite you to present your strategic plans and your key performance targets.

69
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:43,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Iniimbitahan namin kayong tulungan-punan ang hinihingi ng ordinaryong Pilipino sa DOJ,

70
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:49,880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: isang sistema ng katarungan na gumagana, agad, mahusay at patas.

71
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:56,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Lalo na at pagkain, kabuhayan, kaligtasan at kinabukasan

72
00:11:57,420 --> 00:12:19,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ng mga anak natin ang nakataya. We look forward to a productive and candid discussion. Paano ma-o-optimize itong proposed allocation? Paano pa maidadagdag at saan natin kukunin ang idadagdag para magampanan ang mga mandato ng may pinakamataas na antas ng pananagutan, accountability, at transparency?

73
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:24,240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We now ask Senator Lacson for his opening statement. You have the floor, sir.

74
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:27,420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: None from this representation, Mr. Chairman.

75
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:38,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: With that, we can now proceed. Secretary Vida, you have the floor for your opening statement and your presentation. Go ahead, sir.

76
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:48,640
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Magandang umaga po at maraming salamat po sa pagkakataon. Ako po ang inyong Secretary of Justice, Frederick A. Vida.

77
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:56,840
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Kasama ko po ang iba't-ibang opisyalis at lingkodbayan mula sa pamilya ng Department of Justice.

78
00:12:56,840 --> 00:13:06,540
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: At para po sa batid na kaalaman ng lahat, ang sampu po na attached agencies ng Department of Justice ay unang-una,

79
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:16,240
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: ang Office of the Solicitor General, ang ating pong Bureau of Corrections, ang Bureau of Immigration, ang Land Registration Authority,

80
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:18,240
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: ang National Bureau of Investigations.

81
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:31,020
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Ang Office of the Government Corporate Council, ang Parole and Probation Administration, ang ating pong PCGG, Presidential Commission on Good Government,

82
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:39,560
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: and ang ating pong Public Attorney's Office, at syempre po kasama rin po natin ng Office of the Alternative Dispute Resolutions.

83
00:13:40,180 --> 00:13:47,900
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Salamat po, ginagalang at minamahal na aming Senador, Senator Francis Pangilinan, and Senator Ping Lacson.

84
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:59,480
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Salamat po sa pagkakataon para amin pong maihain at maidulog ang proposed budget ng DOJ for 2027.

85
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:13,760
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Ito po, para pong sa bilang ay malaki, 46 billion, ito po ay 0.64% lamang ng kabuang budget para sa susunod na taon ng national government.

86
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:16,760
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: At kasama ko po ang iba't-ibang undersecretary.

87
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:24,880
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Assistant Secretary, kami po ay handa na tugunan lahat ng inyong katanungan at paglilinaw.

88
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:27,160
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: At maraming salamat po sa pagkakataon.

89
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:31,700
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Sa pagpapatuloy po ng aming pong paghain, ng aming proposed budget,

90
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:38,160
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Nandito po ang aming kasama, si Undersecretary Anika Gran-Ong, para ho ipagpatuloy ang aming presentasyon.

91
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,400
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Maraming salamat po.

92
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:44,260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead, Yusek, you have the floor.

93
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:45,840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Annika ba yan? Annika?

94
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:46,520
DOJ Undersecretary Majken Anika S. Gran-Ong: Yes, sir.

95
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:48,800
DOJ Undersecretary Majken Anika S. Gran-Ong: Good morning.

96
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:53,400
